## IN FLIGHT — nothing here is settled

1. **Sweep-cost probe re-running** to `results/timings_clean.json`
   (`scripts/time_cells.py`, SWE males = the 269-year panel, so upper
   bounds). The earlier `results/timings.json` was DELETED as contaminated —
   two overlapping runs mixed pre- and post-GP-fix numbers. Do not trust any
   quoted timing that does not come from the clean file.
   Reliable so far, same code state: classical cells 0.2–15 s; neural
   ensembles ~640–830 s/cell; NB native ~85–120 s. `scripts/sweep_cost.py`
   turns the file into per-regime wall time.
2. **The full grid may not be affordable on this machine.** Classical 5x5 is
   ~minutes per regime; the neural axis is 3 orders of magnitude worse and
   `GP/split_conf` hit a 1.4 GB allocation failure at least once. Options
   (reduce `n_median_samples` for GP, cap the GP's training window, run
   neural on the high-RAM server, drop cells to secondary) are NOT decided.
   If the GP window is capped: note a trailing 40-year window was measured
   scoring BETTER than the full 269 (rmse 0.65 vs 1.19) **before** any cap
   was chosen — so a cap justified by score would be outcome-driven. Justify
   on feasibility and the source paper (Huynh–Ludkovski use 27 years) or not
   at all, and disclose the prior observation.
3. **Age-support comparability is an OPEN defect in the analysis stage.**
   A synthetic end-to-end run put `CBD/native` alone in the MCS — CBD is fit
   on ages 55+, so its CRPS mean is over 45 ages while LC/PLC average over
   100. `losses_from_rows` restricts to common CELLS (addendum 3 §11) but
   not to a common AGE SUPPORT. Cross-family score comparisons are not yet
   apples-to-apples. Fix before any real-data ranking is reported.

## Rules that are easy to break

- Real-data runs need `allow_real=True` — the auditable act, kept
  deliberately.
- Never clip SVAR rates or Poisson means to rescue a divergent draw
  (addendum 3 §7): rejection only, or divergence silently becomes a
  flattering bounded interval.
- `runner.py`'s `obs_full` keeps the 1e-10 rate floor ON PURPOSE — the
  half-count there shifts ISL female 2020 e0 by −0.370 y, past gate 3's
  0.15 y tolerance (addendum 3 §5 documents the split convention).
- Losses are never imputed: `mortcal.inference` RAISES on non-finite input.
  It used to invert the MCS silently under exactly the NaN pattern the
  runner produces.
- Do NOT resume workflow `wf_75bb90b5-839` (dead; clobbers manual fixes).
- Do not commit `results/parity/D_*.csv` / `E_*.csv` (raw HMD, gitignored).

