- Pre-addendum-2 coverage of a *correctly specified* model: 0.104 / 0.189 /
  0.278 against nominal 0.50 / 0.80 / 0.95.
- Conformal scored from sample quantiles vs its own bounds: marginal/joint
  0.995/0.957 vs 0.960/0.740 — the H3 gap understated 6x.
- Structural zeros in the shift training panel: 99 cells, 7 (pop,sex), ages
  95–99, every one D=0 with Jan-1 population 0 at both Lexis corners.
- Zero-death test cells 2020–24, sex-specific: ISL f 117 (23.4%), LUX f 110
  (22.0%). NOT 52/10.4% — that was HMD's Total column, which is never
  modelled.
- Schnürch–Korn (2022) Table 3, the stable-regime prior art H2 must be
  framed against: LC10 74.0, LC20 74.3, ACF 77.2, RNN 86.0, FFNN 97.0,
  CNN 98.0 PICP at nominal 95%, ages 60–89, 2007–2016.

## TRAP ADDED 2026-08-27 (afternoon) — drive letter G: vs H:

The external volume mounts as **G:** in some sessions and **H:** in others.
`.venv` bakes absolute paths; `uv run` (even `--no-sync`) sees a path
mismatch, silently REMOVES the venv and recreates it EMPTY — that happened
today and cost a full `uv sync --group neural`. Before anything: check
`Get-PSDrive` and use the letter the venv was built under, or resync once.
Also: uv here is 0.11.19 under the Gaming profile, not 0.12.5.
GP/split_conf OOM (1.59 GB) reproduces SOLO — it is the wrapper's
`n_median_samples=1000` rsample on the GP posterior, not contention.

## LAUNCH PLAN (2026-08-27, afternoon) — how the real-data sweeps run

`scripts/run_regime.py <regime> --out results/<regime>.parquet --jobs 12
--exclude-models GP` then a second pass `--models GP --jobs 2`. Reason: the
per-cell probe timings are WALL seconds of a single multi-threaded process,
so a serial sweep is 2.17 h/triple wall (shift = 87 h). Parallelism is per
population (one process each, BLAS/torch pinned to ONE thread in
_worker_init so 12 jobs on 12 cores do not oversubscribe — the 2.2x
inflation in results/timings.json came from overlapping multi-threaded
runs). GP cells need ~1.6 GB each on 15.7 GB RAM -> their own pass at low
parallelism. Parts land in results/<regime>.parts/<POP>.parquet and a
killed run resumes by skipping existing parts. Device: MORTCAL_DEVICE
(default cpu); GPU only if the A/B probe (results/timings_gpu.json vs
timings_cached.json) shows a real gain.

